# Deploy Node.js Website on AWS EC2 in Windows (Without PuTTY)

You can do everything using only:

* Command Prompt / PowerShell
* OpenSSH (already built into Windows 10/11)

---

# STEP 1: Create Node.js Project

## Create Folder

```cmd id="0u3jlwm"
mkdir mywebsite
cd mywebsite
```

---

## Initialize Project

```cmd id="fs72yq"
npm init -y
```

---

## Install Express

```cmd id="9p6lkk"
npm install express
```

---

## Create `server.js`

```javascript id="4rvjlwm"
const express = require('express');

const app = express();

app.use(express.static('public'));

app.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

---

## Create Public Folder

```cmd id="bhm0bq"
mkdir public
```

Create `index.html` inside public:

```html id="jlwm4g"
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Website</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hello AWS 🚀</h1>
</body>
</html>
```

---

# STEP 2: Run Locally

```cmd id="p1u97q"
node server.js
```

Open:

```text id="jlwmqq"
http://localhost:3000
```

---

# STEP 3: Create AWS EC2

Go to:

[AWS EC2 Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Create:

* Ubuntu instance
* t2.micro
* Allow:

  * SSH (22)
  * Custom TCP (3000)

Download:

```text id="nlxjlwm"
test.pem
```

Move `test.pem` to:

```text id="pkhjlwm"
C:\Users\YOURNAME\Downloads
```

---

# STEP 4: Open PowerShell

Go to Downloads folder:

```powershell id="jlwm4y"
cd Downloads
```

---

# STEP 5: Connect to EC2

Run:

```powershell id="jlwm5z"
ssh -i test.pem ubuntu@YOUR-PUBLIC-IP
```

Example:

```powershell id="jlwm7n"
ssh -i test.pem ubuntu@13.62.105.62
```

Type:

```text id="jlwm6u"
yes
```

Now EC2 terminal opens 🎉

---

# STEP 6: Install Node.js in EC2

Inside EC2:

```bash id="jlwm9o"
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nodejs npm -y
```

---

# STEP 7: Upload Project from Windows to EC2

Open NEW PowerShell window.

Go where your project exists:

```powershell id="8r1jlwm"
cd path\to\mywebsite
```

Example:

```powershell id="jlwm8w"
cd Desktop
```

Upload project:

```powershell id="jlwm2e"
scp -i C:\Users\YOURNAME\Downloads\test.pem -r mywebsite ubuntu@YOUR-PUBLIC-IP:/home/ubuntu/
```

Example:

```powershell id="jlwm0f"
scp -i C:\Users\Abhishek\Downloads\test.pem -r mywebsite ubuntu@13.62.105.62:/home/ubuntu/
```

---

# STEP 8: Run Project on EC2

Go back to EC2 terminal:

```bash id="jlwm3s"
cd mywebsite
npm install
node server.js
```

---

# STEP 9: Open Website

Browser:

```text id="jlwm1t"
http://YOUR-PUBLIC-IP:3000
```

Example:

```text id="jlwm5m"
http://13.62.105.62:3000
```

Your website is LIVE on AWS 🚀
